{#-
  Video-generation prompt for one beat.

  Structure follows what current text-to-video models respond to best:
    1. Subject + action first (models weight early tokens most)
    2. Wardrobe / character detail
    3. Environment
    4. Camera + lens
    5. Lighting + colour
    6. Style + quality anchors

  Keep it one dense paragraph. Bulleted prompts get flattened by most APIs and
  the ordering signal is lost.
-#}
{{ beat.action }}. {{ cast_description }}.
{% if beat.role == 'hook' %}The very first frame is already mid-motion — no fade in, no empty stage, the subject fills the centre of a vertical frame and looks straight at the lens.
{% elif beat.role == 'switch' %}The energy changes sharply on this beat — a new rhythm, a new angle, a visible surprise.
{% elif beat.role in ('payoff', 'payoff_loop') %}This is the funniest moment of the clip; expressions are big, timing is snappy.
{% elif beat.role == 'loop' %}Ends in exactly the pose the clip opened on so the video restarts seamlessly.
{% endif -%}
Scene: {{ concept.setting_label }}, {{ theme_description }}.
Camera: {{ beat.camera_prompt }}, vertical 9:16 framing, subject centred with headroom.
Lighting: {{ concept.lighting }}.
Colour: {{ concept.palette_label }}.
{% if concept.effects %}Visual effects: {{ concept.effects | join(', ') }}.
{% endif -%}
Motion: smooth {{ music.bpm }} BPM rhythm, movements land on the beat, fluid natural animal locomotion, no stutter, no morphing limbs.
Style: {{ style.render_style }}, {{ style.quality_anchor }}, adorable, wholesome, family-friendly, bright and high-contrast so it reads on a phone screen.
